<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Barrow I. oil field not shut by cyclone - WAPET.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Barrow I. oil field not shut by cyclone - WAPET.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Barrow Island oil field offshore Western Australia will not be forced to shut-in production by tropical cyclone Phil, a West Australian Petroleum Pty Ltd (WAPET) spokesman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>WAPET had started to shut-in the field as Phil approached but production was now getting back to normal as the cyclone weakened, he said from Perth.</p>
<p>He said Barrow Island's current output was about 13,000 barrels per day.</p>
</text>
